    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.misc, mini.animate\n\n### Description\n\nBasically, during scrolling animation in ``:lua MiniMisc.zoom()`` mode, the commandline renders at the center of the screen till the scroll animation is done.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.11.0-dev-1341+g5eda7aafe9\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```lua\r\nvim.env.LAZY_STDPATH = \".repro\"\r\nload(vim.fn.system(\"curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/folke/lazy.nvim/main/bootstrap.lua\"))()\r\n\r\nrequire(\"lazy.minit\").repro({\r\n\tspec = {\r\n\t\t\"echasnovski/mini.animate\",\r\n\t\t\"echasnovski/mini.misc\",\r\n\t},\r\n})\r\n\r\nvim.o.number = true\r\n\r\nrequire(\"mini.animate\").setup()\r\nrequire(\"mini.misc\").setup()\r\n```\r\n1. Open a file which is big enough to be scrollable for atleast 2 seconds with the following command ``nvim -u repro.lua bigfile.lua``.\r\n2. Run the command ``:lua MiniMisc.zoom()``.\r\n3. type ``ggG`` in normal mode to scroll from top of the file to bottom of the file. You can see that command line is rendered at the center of the screen during scrolling.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nCommandline should not be rendered at the center of the screen during scrolling animation.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nCommandline is rendered at the center of the screen during scrolling animation.",
