            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Thanks for the issue!\r\n> \r\n> I can not reproduce. In particular, because \"Open a file which is big enough to be scrollable for atleast 2 seconds ...\" is not really possible with the provided 'init.lua' as it defines 250 milliseconds total scroll time.\r\n> \r\n> Even with 'mini.animate' configured to have scroll of 2000 milliseconds, it is still not reproducible.\r\n> \r\n> What makes you think that this is command line that is rendered on top? Could you make a screencast, please?\r\n\r\nI apologize for not actually uploading a screencast earlier since without it this bug wouldn't make sense and is ridiculous.\r\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1ljBqCHl2V3PJ1Z_TujeXWgurYYMCew4r/view?usp=sharing\r\nI am posting the google drive link since the video is over 10mb and github is not allowing me to upload.\r\n\r\nBut in this video you can see that ``:lua MiniMisc.zoom()`` appears in the middle of the screen while scrolling. By cmdline appearing in middle, that is what I meant.\r\n\r\nAs for the file used in scrolling\r\nhttps://github.com/231tr0n/config/blob/main/nvim/init.lua\r\nrepro.lua is the same as above. With this setup I am able to reproduce it.",
